    "result": "Perfect! Let me create a final summary of the implementation. I have successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval` with the following components:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### Core Changes:\n\n**1. `frai-core/src/eval/index.js` - `generateReport` function**\n- Accepts optional `thresholds` object parameter\n- For each threshold, finds the metric and compares score against minimum\n- Handles null scores correctly (they fail the threshold)\n- Adds `passed` field and `thresholds` array to report when thresholds are provided\n- Works with both default and custom metrics\n\n**2. `frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js` - Report formatting**\n- JSON: unchanged (includes the new report fields automatically)\n- Markdown: adds \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL status for each threshold\n\n**3. `frai-cli/src/index.ts` - CLI integration**\n- Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (repeatable)\n- Validation:\n  - Format: `^([a-z_]+)=([0-9.]+)$`\n  - Range: 0 \u2264 value \u2264 1\n  - Exit 2 on malformed threshold\n- Metric validation against evaluated metrics (exit 2 if unknown)\n- Exit codes:\n  - 0: all thresholds pass (or none specified)\n  - 1: any threshold fails\n  - 2: usage error\n\n**4. Tests**\n- 3 new comprehensive tests for threshold functionality\n- All passing \u2713\n\n**5. Documentation**\n- Updated README.md with threshold option documentation\n- Updated eval_harness_design.md with feature notes\n\n### Key Features:\n- \u2705 Works with any metrics (default and custom)\n- \u2705 Null scores fail thresholds (don't crash or pass)\n- \u2705 Report always written, regardless of threshold outcome\n- \u2705 Backward compatible (without `--threshold`, behavior unchanged)\n- \u2705 CI-friendly exit codes for gating pipelines\n\nThe implementation is ready for use in CI/CD pipelines to gate deployments based on evaluation metric thresholds.",
